08 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "bbe41323-bdcb-5854-b702-4569e847d444" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407909 #edb/ref 1081 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407909 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407909 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "c5ef0e88-3d5a-58fe-a094-21c1a2d940b0" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407910 #edb/ref 1081 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407910 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407910 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "d388ffe7-607b-5621-9d65-a25de45df1c1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407911 #edb/ref 1081 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407911 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407911 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "dae716d0-1847-54c9-9892-a356fbf81aea" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407912 #edb/ref 1081 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407912 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407912 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "e4388827-d9f0-5814-8367-e64cdc9001a1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407892 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407898 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407903 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407904 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407907 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407898 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407913 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "50962eb5-13e0-5527-99de-391f22e7ee03" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407891 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407894 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407897 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407899 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407905 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407905 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407914 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "6472838c-210f-5ad0-99a2-67a0bbd5ad6b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407888 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407901 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407906 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407911 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407912 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407901 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407915 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "67bb5409-539d-5019-8102-b7a8fb7859d7" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407889 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407893 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407896 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407900 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407902 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407900 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407916 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "9e246480-5cbb-5dda-adb1-b0ac60280c69" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407890 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407895 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407908 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407909 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407910 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407908 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407917 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "dff19999-9a3e-55e9-8a46-2ed82f902f83" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407914 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105207" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,4]\\to [-3,9]$ which is given by $f(x)=2x+1?$\n\n- $f(-2)=f(4)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is an injection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407918 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd931a87d6a5fb32d10ed931f443a8175f0760eba9fe2fe69336f8f79e9fd68.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $f(2)=2(-2)+1=-3$ and $f(4)=2\\cdot 4+1=9.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[-2,4]$ that map to the same element in $[-3,9].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407913 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105210" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\n- $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$\n- $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=(x-2)^{2}$\n- $h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407919 #edb/ref 1074 "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3 & =2{x}_{2}+3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(3),$ but $1\\ne 3.$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407916 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80384" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b0/b0a08488ba59344033205903ca973870d0b10837295ced970bf307342e6f7241.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-3,3]\\to [-3,0]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(-3)=f(3)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is an injection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c2e3f55-ea9b-5b9e-badf-26b9e5d93c01" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407920 #edb/ref 1074 "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the graph, we have $f(-3)=f(3)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Again, we have $f(-3)=f(3)$ but $-3\\ne 3.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-3,3],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407917 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80370" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7c/7c2f22af3b39c28d885ac490aae190e1b2d4ad55828a552fec031069d6d912a2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(0)=f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58fa3eda-7303-530c-b266-fd43b4b16a9f" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407921 #edb/ref 1074 "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the graph, we have $f(0)=0$ and $f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407922 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407923 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407922 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2530907e-f808-5c7f-87ec-10398577b7b1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407922 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407921 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407923 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407924 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407923 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59126e0e-e63f-5afb-b7f9-fc09c6d03a0e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407923 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407920 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407924 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407926 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407924 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e89881c-dcee-5df4-a41c-0a7ef882a21c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407924 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407918 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407925 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407922 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407925 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d93d6add-1d7b-59c0-9993-38adf9231b4c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407925 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152825 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407926 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f30d20c